# ADA-Marker configuration (all optional in development; see internal/config).
# Copy the values you need into `.env` (gitignored) — `make run` / `make dev` source it.

# --- Core ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#ADAMARKER_ENV=development                # development | production
#ADAMARKER_HTTP_ADDR=:8080
#ADAMARKER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://adamarker:adamarker@localhost:5433/adamarker?sslmode=disable
#ADAMARKER_BLOB_DIR=./data/blobs
#ADAMARKER_HOSTED_DOMAIN=ntu.edu.tw       # Google Workspace hd claim guard

# Graceful-shutdown drain window (F17). On SIGTERM the process stops fetching new
# jobs and lets in-flight ones finish for up to this long before hard-cancelling
# them; an interrupted job is snoozed and re-run on the next start, never recorded
# as a terminal grading failure. Default 5m30s — just above the 5m longest job
# timeout, so a mid-flight vision call is never insta-cancelled. A Go duration
# string. IMPORTANT for systemd: TimeoutStopSec MUST exceed this value, or systemd
# sends SIGKILL mid-drain and the graceful shutdown is lost.
#ADAMARKER_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN=5m30s

# --- Auth ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production can use email magic-link login, Google OAuth, or both. Email login
# uses the allowlisted users table: users enter their email and receive a one-time
# sign-in link landing on /login/email. Opening the link consumes nothing (so a
# mail scanner prefetching it cannot burn the token); clicking "Complete sign-in"
# there posts the token and establishes the normal server-side session. Links
# expire after 15 minutes and are single-use. Set ADAMARKER_APP_BASE_URL when using
# email login in production so links point at the public HTTPS origin.
#
# Google OAuth is optional. If configured, it is still allowlist-checked.
#ADAMARKER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
#ADAMARKER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
#ADAMARKER_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=https://<host>/auth/callback
#ADAMARKER_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@ntu.edu.tw   # seeded as admin if none exists
#ADAMARKER_DEV_LOGIN=1                    # development only; POST /auth/dev-login

# --- Vision LLM providers (docs/DECISIONS.md D11 v1) -----------------------------
# Providers are managed IN THE APP (Providers page): base URL, models, rate limits,
# and API keys (stored encrypted under ADAMARKER_SECRET_KEY_FILE, default
# ./data/secret.key — auto-generated; back it up with the DB).
#
# The keys below are import seeds: on boot, any of them whose provider name is not
# in the app database yet is imported (encrypted) with sensible defaults; after
# that, the app UI owns the row and these lines are ignored. So "paste key here,
# restart" works — and so does deleting the line afterwards.

# OpenRouter — one key, models from many companies (openrouter.ai → Keys).
# Imports as provider "openrouter" (OpenAI-compatible) with a curated shortlist of
# cheap reasoning-capable vision models (see docs/MODELS.md).
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Qwen (DashScope Intl) / DeepSeek — Anthropic-compatible endpoints.
#QWEN_API_KEY=sk-...
#DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# LaTeX transcription export. These defaults are explicit here so a deployment
# that configures Qwen or another provider does not accidentally keep looking for
# the default OpenRouter/Gemini pair. For Qwen use provider=qwen and model=qwen3-vl-plus.
# DeepSeek's current models are text-only and cannot transcribe answer images.
#ADAMARKER_TRANSCRIBE_PROVIDER=openrouter
#ADAMARKER_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# Optional compile gate for exported .tex. Install Tectonic and set its absolute
# path; also run `make report-fonts` and configure ADAMARKER_REPORT_FONT below so
# mixed Traditional Chinese output does not depend on a system-installed font.
# Unset means exports still ship, marked unverified.
#ADAMARKER_TECTONIC_BIN=/absolute/path/to/tectonic

#ADAMARKER_SECRET_KEY_FILE=./data/secret.key

# --- Worker fleet control (docs/DECISIONS.md D26) --------------------------------
# MUST stay unset on a normal deploy. Setting it to 1 is an escape hatch for
# deliberate multi-instance experiments only — it downgrades the single-worker
# advisory lock from fatal to a warning.
#ADAMARKER_ALLOW_MULTIPLE_WORKERS=1

# --- Local OCR (docs/DECISIONS.md D24) ------------------------------------------
# Fully offline first identification rung (filename -> local OCR -> cloud VLM ->
# human). All three are optional and all-or-nothing: set none to leave it off,
# or set all three to enable it — setting only some logs a startup warning and
# leaves it disabled. `make ocr-models` downloads the model + keys dict into
# ./data/ocr/ (gitignored); it does NOT install libonnxruntime.
#ADAMARKER_OCR_MODEL=./data/ocr/ch_PP-OCRv4_rec_infer.onnx
#ADAMARKER_OCR_KEYS=./data/ocr/ppocr_keys_v1.txt
# libonnxruntime must be >= 1.27 (the Go binding needs C API v26, only available
# from onnxruntime 1.27+). Linux: a GitHub release tarball from
# https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/releases (Ubuntu's apt has no package);
# macOS dev machines: `brew install onnxruntime`.
# Linux (production VM):
#ADAMARKER_ONNXRUNTIME=/opt/onnxruntime/lib/libonnxruntime.so
# macOS (dev):
#ADAMARKER_ONNXRUNTIME=/opt/homebrew/lib/libonnxruntime.dylib

# --- Email (publish + regrade, spec §3, D31) -------------------------------------
# Selects the outbound EmailProvider: file | smtp | postmark | none.
#   file     — writes .eml files under <blobdir>/../outbox (development default).
#   smtp     — STARTTLS (587) or implicit TLS (465) via stdlib net/smtp.
#   postmark — Postmark HTTP API (the plan's intended production provider).
#   none     — records everything, sends nothing; publish marks items "skipped".
# Unset in production defaults to "none" with a loud startup warning (never a
# silent "file", which would drop real student email onto local disk).
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_PROVIDER=file

# File provider only. Override the default outbox directory (sibling of ADAMARKER_BLOB_DIR).
# Development-only escape hatch; the file provider auto-creates the directory if missing.
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_OUTBOX_DIR=./data/outbox

# Required for smtp/postmark (in production, config.Load fails loudly if
# missing for the selected provider).
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_FROM=grader@example.edu

# Inbound domain for the regrade Reply-To address (regrade+<token>@<domain>).
# Unset ⇒ Reply-To is omitted and emails say replies are not monitored.
# NOTE: only the `postmark` provider parses inbound replies. Setting this with the
# `smtp` provider advertises a Reply-To no webhook can receive (the app logs a loud
# startup warning) — use postmark for regrades, or leave this unset under smtp.
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_REPLY_DOMAIN=reply.example.edu

# smtp provider only.
#ADAMARKER_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.edu
#ADAMARKER_SMTP_PORT=587                  # 587 (STARTTLS) or 465 (implicit TLS)
#ADAMARKER_SMTP_USER=
#ADAMARKER_SMTP_PASS=

# postmark provider only — server API token from the Postmark dashboard.
#ADAMARKER_POSTMARK_TOKEN=

# Outbound send rate, sends/sec, applied by the email queue worker. Default 1.0.
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_RATE=1.0

# --- Regrade (spec §4-6, D32-D33, D57) ---------------------------------------------
# How long a signed regrade token stays valid after an email is sent. A Go
# duration string. Default 336h (14 days).
#ADAMARKER_REGRADE_WINDOW=336h

# Regrade v2 turn budget (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-regrade-v2-design.md
# §4, D57): turns 1..MAX are system-adjudicated (each a student reply naming
# contested problems in the <pN> format, each getting a TA-clicked, per-problem
# verdicted result email). Turn MAX+1 — consuming result #MAX's token — hands the
# thread off person-to-person to each contested problem's assigned TA instead of
# producing another adjudication round. Read at receipt time: in-flight tokens
# carry their own turn number, so changing this value mid-term is safe and does
# not reinterpret outstanding tokens. Common values: 2, 3 (default), 5.
#ADAMARKER_REGRADE_MAX=3

# Path secret for POST /webhooks/email/inbound/{secret} — compared constant-time;
# a mismatch 404s (no oracle). MUST be set before wiring a provider's inbound
# webhook to this endpoint; there is no "open" default.
#ADAMARKER_INBOUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Absolute origin of the deployed app (no trailing slash needed — trimmed if
# present). Required for production email-login links; also used to build the
# "open in app" deep link in the regrade v2 final-turn TA-notify handoff email.
# If unset for that handoff email, the link line is dropped entirely rather than
# emitting a dead bare path like "/regrades/42" (dead in any mail client).
#ADAMARKER_APP_BASE_URL=https://ada.csie.ntu.edu.tw

# Temporary HTTPS tunnel testing only: build email-login links from the incoming
# request Host / X-Forwarded-* headers instead of ADAMARKER_APP_BASE_URL. This
# avoids editing .env every time a throwaway tunnel hostname rotates. Do not use
# this for a stable production hostname.
#ADAMARKER_EMAIL_LOGIN_TRUST_REQUEST_HOST=1

# --- Budget cap (trust spec §3, D36) ----------------------------------------------
# Monthly global spend cap compared against month-to-date grading cost_usd (both
# ordinary run leaves AND stricter AI re-grade records, source 'regrade_ai') at run
# creation and at AI-regrade batch time (409 when exceeded). A decimal string
# ("150.50"), never a float — unset means no cap, matching today's unbounded behavior.
#ADAMARKER_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=150.00

# --- Report PDF attachments (report-attachments-regrade-assist spec §3, D42-D45) -------
# Path to a UTF-8 TTF (Noto Sans TC) used to embed CJK glyphs in the per-student result
# PDF/ZIP email attachment. Fetch it with `make report-fonts` (downloads into
# ./data/fonts/, never committed). Feature-gated like local OCR but as a single knob:
# UNSET means the report/attachment feature is off entirely — the publish dialog
# disables the attachment options with a hint, and publish without attachments still
# works either way.
#ADAMARKER_REPORT_FONT=./data/fonts/NotoSansTC-Regular.ttf

# Optional Typst renderer for the result PDF (typst-report spec 2026-07-20): when set
# (and ADAMARKER_REPORT_FONT is configured), LaTeX math in criterion names and problem
# comments — the grading template mandates "LaTeX for math" — is typeset via the mitex
# Typst package instead of appearing as raw \frac{...} source. Any compile failure
# falls back to the built-in fpdf renderer, so sends never fail on this. One-time
# setup: install typst (e.g. `brew install typst`, >= 0.13) and let the FIRST compile
# fetch @preview/mitex into the local package cache (needs network once per machine;
# air-gapped hosts can pre-seed the cache dir or set --package-path via TYPST env vars).
#ADAMARKER_TYPST_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/typst
